CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F307A1785309491
OL,3,CDuke of Sussex's case against Mail
OL,4,Cpublisher to return to court after
OL,5,Cruling
OL,7,FIn his ruling, Mr Justice Nicklin
OL,8,Fsaid: "In substance, the claimants'
OL,9,Fcase invites the court to conclude
OL,10,Fthat, because the information was
OL,11,Fprivate and because Associated cannot
OL,12,Fpositively explain how it was sourced,
OL,13,Fthe article must have been unlawfully
OL,14,Fsourced.
OL,16,F"That is not a permissible approach."
OL,18,FPaul Dacre, the ANL editor-in-chief
OL,19,Fand former editor of the Daily Mail,
OL,20,Fsaid the "trumped-up action" "should
OL,21,Fnever have been brought to trial".
